Subject: Nightingale Update - Priority One

Agent Kepler,

Received your comm regarding the Bucharest anomaly. Situation is…complicated. The “collector,” as locals refer to him, isn’t dealing in antiquities as initially reported. It’s biological material. Specifically, highly modified avian DNA. Think accelerated evolution, weaponized migratory patterns. The samples aren’t just from local species; we’ve identified genetic markers from birds native to the Amazon, Siberia, even extinct species. He’s building something, and it’s not a museum exhibit.

My cover as a ornithological researcher is holding, barely. The collector, a man named Volkov, is meticulous. Surveillance is a nightmare; he anticipates countersurveillance with unnerving accuracy. He operates out of a seemingly abandoned textile factory on the outskirts of the city. Access is heavily guarded, not by conventional security, but by a network of trained raptors. Yes, you read that correctly. Hawks, falcons, even a golden eagle. They’re not just guards; they’re integrated into the security system – pressure plates, infrared triggers, the works. I’ve observed them responding to vocal commands, complex sequences. It’s… disturbing.

I managed to acquire a partial schematic of the factory layout during a “chance” encounter with a disgruntled former employee. It’s a labyrinth. The core of the operation appears to be located deep underground, shielded from electromagnetic interference. I suspect he’s using the factory’s old ventilation system for air filtration and containment. The air smells…wrong. A metallic tang, overlaid with something organic and faintly sweet.

My current assessment is that Volkov isn’t working alone. There’s a secondary contact, a woman identified as Dr. Anya Petrova. She’s a geneticist, formerly associated with a defunct Soviet bio-weapons program. I’ve been attempting to establish a connection, posing as a fellow researcher interested in her published work, but she’s proving elusive. She only appears at the factory briefly, usually late at night.

Requesting immediate authorization for a full-scale extraction and containment operation. This isn’t just about stopping a black market trade; this is a potential bioweapon threat of significant magnitude. The implications of weaponized avian evolution are… catastrophic. We need to secure the samples, neutralize Volkov and Petrova, and determine the extent of their network. 

I’m operating on limited resources and increasingly exposed. My cover is fragile. I need backup, and I need it now. A team specializing in avian countermeasures would be invaluable. 

Awaiting your orders.

Nightingale.



